            "question": "Do I need a permit for a rooftop deck railing in East Austin?",
            "answer": "<p>A new rooftop deck is new construction, so expect a City of Austin building permit and an inspection. The code sets a 36\" minimum guard height for a single-family house; the 33.6\" panel gives 36\". Replacing an existing roof-deck railing may be handled differently, so ask first. On a roof, the attachment must work with the membrane; plan it with your roofer and send photos of the roof edge.</p>",
